<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Community Is Famous For... – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 16px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Community News</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Our Community Is Famous For...</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Exchange information on familiar topics with peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can describe community members featured in local news using physical traits and personality adjectives (e.g., 'The reporter has short black hair and is very friendly.' 'The artisan is tall, wears a Sombrero Pintao, and is very proud of his work.'). Can ask and answer questions about community events and traditions with peers (e.g., 'What did you like about the Carnival in Penonomé?' 'I liked the queen's beautiful outfit and the music.' 'Did you go to the school fair?' 'Yes, I went with my friends.'). Can exchange information with peers about popular landmarks in their community (e.g., 'Isla Colón is a popular landmark in our province.' 'Yes, I went last month and saw a lot of tourists.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 15%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various large pictures of community events and people (e.g., a reporter with a microphone, an artisan wearing a Sombrero Pintao, a Carnival parade, a market, a school fair). Students are asked to call out what they see and if they recognize the event or person. E.g., "What do you see here?" "Is this a reporter or an artisan?" "Did you go to a carnival last year?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher points to a picture of a reporter at a community fair. "Look at this picture. This is a reporter. She has short black hair and is very friendly. Last weekend, she interviewed people at the community fair. I went to the fair too. I liked the music, but I didn't like the loud sounds." The teacher models the pronunciation of past tense -ed endings (e.g., /d/ in 'interviewed,' /t/ in 'liked') and emphasizes descriptive adjectives.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding using questions like:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does the reporter have long hair or short hair?" (Expected: "Short hair.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Was the reporter friendly or serious?" (Expected: "Friendly.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I like the loud sounds?" (Expected: "No, you didn't.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Community News"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Short dialogue between two peers, Mario and Sofia, discussing a recent community festival they both attended. The dialogue will be presented as an audio clip or written on a large poster/projected. It will include descriptions of people and events using the past simple, physical appearance adjectives, and compound sentences with 'but'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Exchanging personal information, sharing past experiences and preferences, describing people and community members.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> Teacher asks: "What community event are Mario and Sofia talking about?" "Who did they see?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students listen/read and determine if statements are true or false. E.g., "Mario liked the music at the festival." "Sofia saw an artisan with black straight hair."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match the community member (e.g., Carnival Queen, artisan) to their description (e.g., 'tall and proud', 'beautiful and friendly') or what they did.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Practice using past simple tense, compound sentences with 'but', and adjectives for describing physical appearance and personality (e.g., 'friendly', 'tall', 'short', 'curly hair', 'black straight hair', 'proud') within the context of community events and news. Focus on pronunciation of -ed endings (/t/, /d/, /ɪd/) and distinguishing short/long vowel sounds (e.g., /æ/ in 'banner' vs. /eɪ/ in 'parade').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion:</b> The teacher provides sentences with blanks based on the Presentation dialogue or new community event descriptions. Students verbally complete the sentences in pairs, using target vocabulary and grammar. E.g., "The _______ (reporter / artist) _______ (interview / decorated) the banner." "The Carnival Queen had _______ (curly / black straight) hair and was very _______ (excited / shy)." Teacher circulates, providing feedback on accuracy and pronunciation.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Picture Description Chain:</b> The teacher shows a series of picture cards depicting different community members or scenes from events (e.g., an artisan creating a Sombrero Pintao, students preparing a mural, a colorful Carnival float). Students work in small groups. One student describes a picture using past simple and descriptive adjectives (e.g., "She is an artisan. She has curly hair and is very proud. She prepared a Sombrero Pintao last week."). The next student adds to the description or describes the next picture, incorporating 'but' if expressing a preference (e.g., "I liked the Sombrero Pintao, but I prefer the colorful Pollera."). The teacher prompts for different adjectives and ensures correct verb forms and pronunciation of /t/, /d/, /ɪd/.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - Q&A about Shared Experiences:</b> Students work in pairs. They are given a list of common community events (e.g., school fair, local festival, market visit) and a list of descriptive adjectives/nouns. Students take turns asking and answering questions about past attendance and experiences. E.g., "Did you go to the school fair last month?" "Yes, I went. I saw a reporter there. He was tall and friendly. He interviewed my friend." "What did you like about it?" "I liked the games, but I didn't like the long line for food."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Community News"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Role-play: "Our Community News Interview." Students work in pairs. One student acts as a "reporter" from 'Our Community News,' and the other is a "community member" who recently attended a local event (e.g., a festival, a parade, a community fair, or visited a landmark). Each pair will choose an event or landmark from their community (real or imagined) to discuss.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students receive role cards (Reporter / Community Member) and a scenario prompt (e.g., "Interview about the Desfile de las Mil Polleras," "Interview about a visit to Isla Colón").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The "reporter" asks the "community member" questions about their past experience at the event/landmark. E.g., "Good morning! Did you participate in the Desfile de las Mil Polleras last weekend?" "Who did you see there?" "What did you like about the parade?" "How did the Carnival Queen look?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The "community member" responds, describing people they saw (physical traits, personality), events that happened, and expressing their likes/dislikes, incorporating past simple tense, descriptive adjectives, and compound sentences with 'but'. E.g., "Yes, I went with my family. I saw many women in beautiful Polleras. The artisan near the market was tall and proud; he made wonderful Sombreros Pintaos. I liked the music, but I didn't like the long walk."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students practice their role-play for 5-7 minutes.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist. The teacher uses a simple checklist to observe pairs as they perform their role-plays, noting students' use of target grammar, vocabulary, and communicative functions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each pair performs their "Our Community News Interview" role-play for the teacher or a small group of peers. The teacher listens actively and uses the checklist to note performance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (especially of past tense -ed endings and vowel sounds).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of past simple tense.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of descriptive adjectives (physical appearance, personality).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to ask and answer questions about past events.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of 'but' to express preferences or soft disagreement.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborative interaction and exchange of information.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I learned about describing people from my community news report was..."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new word I used today was... (e.g., 'artisan', 'proud', 'curly hair')."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of describing community events or people in English was easy for me today?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part was challenging, and how can I improve my speaking?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this speaking lesson? (e.g., Students were engaged in role-playing, they used target vocabulary and past simple correctly for the most part, pronunciation practice was effective).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., Some students struggled with irregular past tense verbs, need more practice with 'but' to express differing opinions, ensure all students participate actively in pair work).</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This speaking lesson provided students with fluency practice in describing past community events and people. In Lesson 4 (Writing), students will build on these spoken ideas to write a short news report or descriptive paragraph about a community event, applying the same grammar and vocabulary in written form.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>